{
  "scene_id": "scene.book003.009_stalemate_departure_the_first_coming.scene003",
  "description": "@scene_id: scene.book003.009_stalemate_departure_the_first_coming.scene003",
  "entities": [],
  "locations": [
    {
      "id": "unknown",
      "name": "Unknown",
      "description": "Location: Realm/Physical/Unknown",
      "path": "Realm/Physical/Unknown",
      "type": "area"
    }
  ],
  "events": [
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "timestamp": 45,
      "actor": "Eduhauana",
      "action": "speak",
      "data": {
        "text": "\"Departure authorization,\"",
        "line": 54
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "timestamp": 46,
      "actor": "unknown",
      "action": "speak",
      "data": {
        "text": "\"Acknowledged. Flagging indigenous biological management as priority deployment for next convergence. Recommend Nephilim-class assets: genetic engineering optimized for stone-flesh combat, consciousness-disruption capabilities, sufficient quantity for complete suppression.\"",
        "line": 56
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "timestamp": 47,
      "actor": "unknown",
      "action": "speak",
      "data": {
        "text": "\"Approved. Additionally: monitor psychological warfare effectiveness through remote Needle sensor arrays. Document tribal fragmentation progression. Assess optimal timing for Second Coming deployment based on indigenous self-suppression metrics.\"",
        "line": 58
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "timestamp": 54,
      "actor": "Eduhauana",
      "action": "speak",
      "data": {
        "text": "\"Efficient,\"",
        "line": 70
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "timestamp": 55,
      "actor": "unknown",
      "action": "speak",
      "data": {
        "text": "\"And the slaves we leave behind?\"",
        "line": 72
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "timestamp": 56,
      "actor": "unknown",
      "action": "speak",
      "data": {
        "text": "\"The Igigi will continue breeding, maintaining infrastructure, planting psychological weapons they don't know they carry. The Reptilians will provide basic security, prevent indigenous populations from destroying what we've built. Neither species requires our continued presence\u2014they're tools that operate autonomously once properly programmed.\"",
        "line": 74
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "timestamp": 66,
      "actor": "he",
      "action": "speak",
      "data": {
        "text": "\"The indigenous biologicals will celebrate our departure,\"",
        "line": 88
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "timestamp": 67,
      "actor": "Eduhauana",
      "action": "speak",
      "data": {
        "text": "\"Let them believe it,\"",
        "line": 90
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "timestamp": 68,
      "actor": "unknown",
      "action": "speak",
      "data": {
        "text": "\"And three thousand cycles from now?\"",
        "line": 92
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "timestamp": 69,
      "actor": "unknown",
      "action": "speak",
      "data": {
        "text": "\"We return to find them fractured. Weakened. Fighting each other over resources and territories and grievances they can no longer trace to their source. We deploy Nephilim forces, complete the network, and reduce this world from contested to controlled status with minimal additional resource expenditure.\"",
        "line": 94
      }
    }
  ],
